# Product scroll / mobile viewport

## Root cause of the bottom “wipe”

Chrome’s top/bottom bars show and hide while scrolling. That changes the **visual** viewport (`dvh`) without the user changing settings.

The product page **ends on inkwell (VHS)** but used to paint **vellum on html/body/the settled stack**. During bar show/hide or rubber-band, those layers briefly show through → a cream/vellum rectangle “wiping” the screen. JS-retinting them to inkwell only swapped it for a **dark** wipe. `overscroll-behavior` hid the bounce but **blocks pull-to-refresh** — do not use it.

**Permanent fix:** scroll-roots for product are **always inkwell**. Vellum grain is only on **HeaderBar** + the **hero→scent wrapper** in `ProductPage`. Never put page-end color on a class toggle.

## Paint rules (product)

- `html` / `body` / settled stack shell: **solid inkwell-900** (no vellum tile).
- Hero→scent wrapper: **`bg-vellum-paper`**.
- HeaderBar: **`bg-vellum-paper`** (already).
- VHS stage: **inkwell** + **`min-h-lvh`**.
- Do **not** retint settled/body on scroll.
- Do **not** set **`overscroll-behavior`** on product pages.

## Viewport units

- **Scent-anatomy sticky shell**: **`h-dvh min-h-svh`** — play cue above collapsing bottom bar (accept mild layout shift).
- **VHS stage**: **`min-h-lvh`** — fills chrome-hidden viewport; avoid `dvh` (stage shrinks when the bar returns).
- **VHS bloom**: **`lvh`/`lvw`**, never **`vmax`** (bar toggle resizes bloom → fake wipe).
- **Scroll runways / leave `y`**: **`svh`**.

## Overflow / compositing (stack PageTransition)

- Settled stack: **`overflow-x: visible`** on `.page-transition--stack` (ancestor `overflow-x: clip` → sticky jitter, WebKit 247130).
- Clip **only** while `.page-transition--stack-animating`.
- Settled: no `transform`, no `contain: paint`, `will-change: auto`, `position: relative`.
- Sliding covers stay flat cream (`background-image: none`) for iOS; product settled is inkwell as above.
